 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios Mattel shares yesterday took a breather, as investors try to gauge whether the Barbie maker will get bought.

 Catch up quick: Mattel CEO Ynon Kreiz stepped down last week to become co-CEO of Paramount Skydance, succeeded by board member and former Condé Nast boss Roger Lynch.

 That was followed by a WSJ report that PE-backed Authentic Brands Group had made a $6 billion takeover approach. Ariel Investments, which holds a 5.4% stake in Mattel, then became the second activist investor this year to push for a sale — following Southeastern Asset Management back in May. 
 
